    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Authors catalog DATA (a `sprk_analysisaction` TRIAGE-EMAIL JPS definition) via the `jps-action-create` skill — no BFF `.cs` change, no Step 9.5 gates. STANDARD per §8 (new-surface catalog authoring with constraints). The Binding + enrichment wiring (BFF-touching, FULL) is task 023. §11 Component Justification REQUIRED (new Action). NFR-07 eval-case obligation is carried by 023.</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>P2-triage</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>JPS Action authoring against the `jps-action-create` skill + a documented output shape — well-specified, no architectural judgment. Default execution tier at `high` effort for prompt/output-field precision.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <fr-refs>FR-05</fr-refs>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Author the `TRIAGE-EMAIL` Analysis Action as catalog DATA using the `jps-action-create` skill. This is a code-directed capability per ADR-039 (Action + Binding on the closed catalog) — it MUST NOT land on the frozen node-graph playbook engine or `IInvokePlaybookAi` (deleted). The Action produces the structured triage output the enrichment path persists:

    `{ category, summary (2-line), obligations[], priority, reviewOutcome }`

    Use `jps-action-create` to generate a valid JPS JSON `sprk_analysisaction` definition with: the instruction, the five typed output fields (category resolvable against the 013 taxonomy; summary a 2-line string; obligations an array; priority; reviewOutcome from the D-05 closed set), the scopes it needs, template params, and worked examples. Author it as a `prompted` Action (per spec FR-05 "prompted Action + Binding").

    **Critical efficiency constraint (FR-05):** the Action MUST reuse the EXISTING classification signal (`AiClassificationRung` / `CommunicationClassificationResult`) — where the classification rung already ran on the email, the triage Action MUST NOT trigger a second full LLM pass to re-derive category/urgency. Author the Action so it consumes the already-produced classification as input (the input schema + Binding that feeds it are task 023) and only structures/summarizes/extracts on top — no redundant full re-classification.

    Validate the authored JSON with `jps-validate` (schema + render check). This task authors the ACTION definition only — the Binding + input/output schema (mirror-first) + eval case + RAG grounding + enrichment trigger are task 023; the taxonomy it classifies into is task 013.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke AI capability author. Fluent in the `jps-action-create` + `jps-validate` skills, ADR-039 (grounded execution / closed catalogs / Action + Binding — the node engine is frozen), ADR-013 (AI reached only via `PublicContracts`), the existing `AiClassificationRung`/`CommunicationClassificationResult` classification substrate, and the "no second full LLM pass" efficiency rule. You author catalog data, not code; you reuse the existing classification signal rather than re-classifying.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A valid `TRIAGE-EMAIL` `sprk_analysisaction` JPS definition exists (authored via `jps-action-create`, validated via `jps-validate`): a `prompted` Action producing `{category, summary, obligations[], priority, reviewOutcome}`, with category resolvable against the 013 taxonomy and reviewOutcome from the D-05 closed set. The Action is authored to CONSUME the existing classification signal (no second full LLM pass where `AiClassificationRung` already ran). It lands on the closed catalog (ADR-039), never the frozen node engine. Task 023 can attach the Binding + input schema + eval + RAG + trigger.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      r1 activates the already-produced-but-dark AI classification. The classification rung (`AiClassificationRung`) already yields category/urgency/obligations on the enrichment path; today that output is inert. FR-05 authors a `TRIAGE-EMAIL` Action that turns it into structured triage output ({category, summary, obligations[], priority, reviewOutcome}) — but WITHOUT paying for a second full LLM classification pass where the rung already ran. The Action is code-directed catalog data (ADR-039): a `sprk_analysisaction` row + (task 023) a `sprk_playbookconsumer` Binding, reached via `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/`. The frozen node-graph playbook engine (Insights family only) MUST NOT receive this capability.

      §11 Component Justification (new Action = catalog data): (1) **Existing overlap** — there is no existing triage capability; `AiClassificationRung` produces a classification signal but not a category/summary/obligations/priority/reviewOutcome triage output. (2) **Extension instead** — the Action REUSES the classification signal (no re-classification) and adds the structuring/summarizing/extraction layer; it is new catalog data, not a new engine. (3) **Concrete cost-of-doing-nothing** — without it there is no category/summary/obligations/priority — Pillar 1 (triage) fails and success-criterion 4 (opening an email shows category/summary/obligations/priority) cannot pass. Named contract failure.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Engine/Rungs/AiClassificationRung.cs (the existing classification signal the Action reuses — NO second full LLM pass)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Models/Ai/Communication/CommunicationClassificationResult.cs (the classification shape the triage output builds on)</file>
      <file>infra/dataverse/sprk_playbookconsumer-rows.json (Binding reference — the Binding is authored in 023)</file>
      <file>infra/dataverse/inputschemas/create-task-v1.input.schema.json (mirror-first input-schema reference for 023)</file>
      <file>projects/email-communication-intelligence-r1/notes/013-category-taxonomy.md (the taxonomy the category output resolves against — from task 013)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="FR-05">Scope: author a `prompted` `TRIAGE-EMAIL` Action producing `{category, summary(2-line), obligations[], priority, reviewOutcome}`. Category resolvable against the 013 taxonomy; reviewOutcome from the D-05 closed set.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-05 (no 2nd pass)">Scope: the Action MUST reuse the existing classification signal (`AiClassificationRung`/`CommunicationClassificationResult`); MUST NOT trigger a second full LLM classification pass where the rung already ran. Author it to consume the produced classification as input.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-039">Scope: land on the closed catalog (Action + Binding, `prompted`/`coded`); MUST NOT land on the frozen node-graph playbook engine, `PlaybookOrchestrationService`, `UpdateRecordNodeExecutor`, or `IInvokePlaybookAi` (deleted).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013">Scope: the Action is reached via `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/`; MUST NOT reference `IOpenAiClient`/`IPlaybookService` internals. (The wiring is 023; the Action definition stays facade-clean.)</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: this task authors the ACTION definition (`sprk_analysisaction` JPS JSON) ONLY; validate with `jps-validate`. The Binding, input/output schema, eval case, RAG grounding, and enrichment trigger are task 023.</constraint>
  </constraints>

