  <justification>
    <existing>No triage capability exists; `AiClassificationRung` produces a classification signal but not the {category, summary, obligations[], priority, reviewOutcome} triage output.</existing>
    <extension>The Action reuses the existing classification signal (no re-classification) and adds a structuring/summarizing/extraction layer as new catalog data (ADR-039) — not a new engine, not a second LLM pass.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without it there is no category/summary/obligations/priority triage output — Pillar 1 fails and success-criterion 4 (opening an email shows category/2-line summary/obligations/priority) cannot pass. Concrete contract failure.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read spec FR-05 + `AiClassificationRung.cs` + `CommunicationClassificationResult.cs` + the 013 taxonomy note + `ai-guide-consumer-wiring.md` / `SPAARKE-PLAYBOOK-LLM-OUTPUT-PATTERN.md` to fix the output shape, the reuse-the-signal contract, and the D-05 reviewOutcome closed set.</step>
    <step order="2">Invoke `jps-action-create` to author the `TRIAGE-EMAIL` `sprk_analysisaction` JPS JSON: instruction; five typed output fields ({category resolvable against 013 taxonomy, summary 2-line, obligations[], priority, reviewOutcome from D-05 set}); scopes; template params; worked examples. Author `prompted`. Structure the instruction so it consumes the produced classification (no second full pass).</step>
    <step order="3">Validate the authored JSON with `jps-validate` (schema conformance + render check); fix any validation errors.</step>
    <step order="4">Record the authored Action (id/name, output fields, the reuse-the-signal note, the D-05 reviewOutcome set) in `notes/022-triage-email-action.md` for task 023's Binding + eval + trigger, and the §11 justification.</step>
    <step order="5">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (022 ✅) + `current-task.md`; confirm 023 (Binding/schema/eval/RAG/trigger), 024, 025 unblocked and point them at the note.</step>
  </steps>

  <tools>
